# LabMail conventions

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/01-architecture.md` before changing code.

- Product: LabMail. Binary: `labmaild`. Module: `github.com/hilather/go-lab-maildev`.
- Receive-only SMTP sink. Never implement working outbound relay or auto-relay.
- Domain logic lives in `internal/app`. REST, MCP, WebSocket, and UI are adapters.
- Do not call REST from MCP or MCP from REST.
- Captured mail is ephemeral. Bootstrap YAML is read-only desired listen/auth/limits.
- Unknown config fields are errors. Relay flags/keys are compile-time failures.
- Prefer Go stdlib and small libraries. Hide third-party SMTP/MIME/MCP types behind adapters.
- Documentation and `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` ship in the same change as the behavior.
